# ripgrep — read via RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH (set in env/common.sh), by rg at the
# shell and by Emacs's `:rg' (xref) alike.
#
# Hidden files are searched -- dotfiles are half of what is looked for here --
# except git's own directory.  A repository's .gitignore keeps out the rest.
# Long lines are shown whole: an Org paragraph is one line, and a match in it
# cut to "[Omitted long line]" is a match that cannot be read.

--smart-case
--hidden
--glob=!.git/*
